    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\n`AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 the pipeline step (`assignCustomerCode` in `owners.POST.yml`) that stamps the owner's `customerCode` before it's saved.\n\nPreviously it computed the code as `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and set it directly. Now it:\n\n1. Computes the same base code (`region + \"-\" + hash8`).\n2. Gathers all existing owners' `customerCode` values from `OwnerRepository.findAll()` (injected by type, matching the style of `CountNamesakes`/`CountHouseholdMembers` in the same package).\n3. If the base collides, appends `-<n>` starting at `n = 2` and incrementing until the code is unique \u2014 so the first collision becomes `-2`, the next `-3`, etc.\n4. Sets the de-duplicated code on the owner.\n\nThe step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]` (already wired), and it reads the existing owners before the new owner is saved, so the new owner isn't counted against itself.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
